  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="6108-7c0b-fe64-5285" name="Arabs and Saracens (Armies of Antiquity) - List Notes" publicationId="aab0-aa1e-0319-4ffe" hidden="false">
      <description>ARABS AND SARACENS ARMY LIST (Armies of Antiquity, pp.32-33), AD 630 - 1300.
Characters: the army may have a General and an Army Battle Standard. Cavalry up to three quarters of the points; Infantry at least a quarter; Special Units up to a quarter, with one elephant per 1,000 points.
Bedouin and Turkish Cavalry: cavalry in the list may turn without penalty during their move and change formation once during movement by any number of ranks at no penalty (including while marching). All bow-armed Turkish cavalry (Askaris, Ghulams, Mamluks and Turkish light cavalry) may make a normal move immediately after shooting in the shooting phase (Parthian Shot; not a charge reaction; may not march).
Combined Formations: where specified, archers may be combined with other infantry in one regiment, in the rear ranks, losing light infantry status; casualties are taken from the other infantry first.

ARMY COMPOSITION (percentages by points):
  Cavalry: up to 75%
  Infantry: at least 25%
  Special Units: up to 25%</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
